 "derivation": "Rig key at Blender (0.0862,-0.0523,2.4) -> three (0.0862,2.4,0.0523); cast (0,0.5,1) -> (0,1,-0.5); re-anchor delta=headCentre-castThree; key head-relative (0.0862,1.4,0.5523) (readback). From the eye the key sits ~70deg overhead. Convex-mirror sub-stellar point S=C+r*(V+K)/|V+K| with Gullstrand r=7.8mm (fit gives the 12.24mm globe, resid <0.25mm, so curvature uses 7.8 and the apex comes from the fit). Predicted key spot = upper limbus, under the upper lid; its visible remainder plus panel-edge streak stay <25 L*. The >=25 set is the frontal wash ring (wash_ny frontal at eye level, 16.94 radiance): static under a +0.5m key shift (G2 directionCos<0), Fresnel-skewed toward the lower limbus (measured 8-22px below sub-stellar points vs 10-24px tolerances). Restoring RoomEnvironment reproduces PRE bit-identically: the module alone moves the reflection.",
